## The Rules Preamble

When you export from TweakLens with "Include project rules" checked, the AI gets a preamble like:

> *Follow the repo's AGENTS.md. Use the existing branding design system (buttonClass, cardRadius, theme tokens) — never hardcode raw colors. Follow Tailwind + responsive conventions (sm:/md:/lg:). Run typecheck + lint + check-docs after changes.*

This is what keeps the AI from:
- Hardcoding colors instead of using your design system's tokens
- Breaking responsive layouts
- Introducing type errors or lint violations
- Touching files it shouldn't

**Always leave it checked unless you know what you're doing.**

---

## Do You Need to Explain "What TweakLens Is" to the AI?

**No!** You don't need to waste time explaining what TweakLens is. The AI only cares about the **instructions**.

You can literally just start a chat like this:

> *"Here is the current code for my screen: [paste code or attach file]*
> 
> *Here is the UI refactor plan I want you to apply:*
> *[paste TweakLens copied text]*
> 
> *Update my code so the visual layout matches these tasks."*

The AI will immediately connect the dots: it finds the old widgets in your code and rewrites them into your new design!
